# Generated by Phase: IMPLEMENT | Feature: EVOL-072, EVOL-070
"""The one contract reader (EVOL-072, EVOL-070): one error code per meaning (DC-36), CRUD-First declared or kept, twice
(DC-37), and the parity of code, contract and test plan (DC-39).

Every contract under contracts/openapi/** and the catalog are read whole — uniqueness and completeness are properties of
the whole. Red when:

  catalog   a code is listed twice (a line scan: YAML keeps the last value); two entries share a meaning (case, spacing
            and punctuation normalised); an entry has no meaning; the catalog is not a mapping of codes.
  codes     a contract names a code (`x-error-codes: [CODE, …]`, anywhere) the catalog lacks, or names codes and no
            catalog exists.
  shape     an operation outside CRUD-First (rules/contract-first-policy.md § CRUD-First) carries no non-empty
            `x-crud-exception: <reason>`. CRUD-shaped: the path, leading `api` / `v<N>…` stripped, alternates literal
            collections and single `{param}`s from a collection; ending in a collection → GET | POST (POST after a param
            is a custom action), ending in a param → GET | PUT | PATCH | DELETE; `…/<collection>/bulk-<verb>` →
            POST | PATCH | DELETE. Search is query parameters, so its path is a collection.
  complete  a resource (a CRUD-shaped collection, or the parent of an item path; a POST-only path after a param with
            nothing below is a custom action, no resource) lacks one of its operations, single and batch — create
            (POST C), list (GET C), read (GET C/{id}), update (PUT | PATCH C/{id}), delete (DELETE C/{id}),
            bulk-create (POST C/bulk-create), bulk-update (PATCH C/bulk-update), bulk-delete (DELETE C/bulk-delete) —
            and its path item (the collection's or an item's) declares no reason: `x-crud-exception: <reason>` for every
            omission, or `{<operation>: <reason>}` per omission.
  baseline  docs/project_log/crud_baseline.json (`undeclared`: the shape and completeness findings older than this law,
            recorded once at SETUP --upgrade from `gate.py contracts --json`) only shrinks: an entry no longer found is
            red (remove it); an entry absent from the base's baseline whose finding the base's contract did not already
            carry is red (declare it — new debt never enters); a baseline git does not track is red.
A contract with no `openapi` / `swagger` / `paths` key (an example payload, a placeholder) is not an OpenAPI document: its
CRUD clauses are not judged, and the note says so. A resource whose path item is a `$ref` lives in another file: not
judged. A path that resolves outside the repository is never read.
  registry  contracts/feature_map.md (the whole table): its table has a `Version` column, and every ACTIVE row whose
            contract carries `info.version` states that version (a `v` prefix allowed); a row naming no file is red.
  tests     (with a base) every operation added since the merge-base carries an `operationId` and is named in the
            `Operation` cell of a TC-API row of some docs/spec/*/test_plan.md — one contract test per operation, planned
            before the build (CONTRACT-FREEZE); `traceability` proves the case has its test, the seal's `red` member
            proves it red at the base.
  statuses  (EVOL-106) each TC-API row's leading Expected Status code(s) are among its Operation's responses
            (`default` and `4XX` cover); and every status literal in a tracked source file — a number in a status
            position (`status_code=`, `.status(…)`, `WriteHeader(…)`, `HTTPException(…)`, …) or a named constant
            read through the stdlib `http.HTTPStatus` phrases (`HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND`, `http.StatusNotFound`,
            `StatusCodes.Status404NotFound`, `status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND`) — is among the responses of the operations
            whose operationId the file names (a file naming none is not judged; tests are not judged). Older code
            findings sit in the baseline as `status:<path>#<code>` and only shrink.
  journey   (with a base) a docs/spec/<F>/test_plan.md changed since the merge-base, whose feature has a user_journey.md,
            carries `### Journey coverage` (`| Paso | Operation |`): every `Paso N` of the journey a row, each cell an
            operationId of the tree or `none — <reason>`. The journey itself names no operation (LAW-16).
An unreadable contract, catalog or baseline is red with its reason (LAW-08). Neither contract nor catalog → `contracts: n/a`.

`parity(repo)` (`gate.py contracts --parity`, the verification-loop member `contract-parity`; it needs a build) runs two
commands of the branch's governed config, with the trust of the project's own test suite (seal.run's boundary):
  observed  the test files under `contracts.tests_root` (default tests/api), run through the seal's own dispatch
            (seal.scoped: each `verification.gates` row with `scoped` gets the files its red_reads hold), with
            `CONTRACT_OBSERVED` naming a fresh folder; each response appends `{"operation": "<operationId>", "status":
            <int>, "code": "<CODE>"|null}` to a `*.jsonl` file there. Red: a failed or timed-out run; no routed test
            file; nothing recorded; a line that is no such object; an unknown operation; an operationId naming two
            operations of one document; a status the operation does not declare (`default` or a range `4XX` covers
            it; a local `$ref` response is read where it points); a code outside the catalog, or outside the
            operation's `x-error-codes` when it lists them; an operation of the tree never observed.
  emitted   `contracts.emit` (`{out}` = a fresh folder) writes the code's own OpenAPI, mirroring contracts/openapi/
            (`{out}/<slug>/v1.json` ↔ contracts/openapi/<slug>/v1.yaml). Both sides are copied without `servers` and
            `tags`, under the authored `openapi` line, then compared by `oasdiff diff --fail-on-diff` (documentation
            and extensions excluded, external refs refused): the operations, the shapes and their constraints,
            `security`, the declared responses, `info.version`. Red: the key null; oasdiff absent (both checked before
            any test runs — parity never passes unproven); the command failing; a twin missing on either side, or two;
            any difference. `contracts.timeout_s` bounds every command (its whole process group).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import copy
import http
import json
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
from pathlib import Path

import unicodedata

from . import documents
from .common import GateFault, clean as _clean, key, parse_yaml, tracked_files
from .freeze import CONTRACT_RE, _load, _parse, _walk
from .frontmatter import _at   # lenient: a base blob that is not UTF-8 reads, never faults
from .seal import _git, _reference, _state_dir, scoped as _scoped, tree_entries, vcfg
from .traceability import is_tracked

CATALOG = "contracts/errors.yaml"
TREE = "contracts/openapi"
BASELINE = "docs/project_log/crud_baseline.json"
OPS = ("get", "put", "post", "delete", "patch")   # head / options carry no CRUD meaning: not judged
PARAM = re.compile(r"\{[^{}/]+\}")
PREFIX = re.compile(r"api|v\d+(?:\.\d+)*(?:(?:alpha|beta)\d*)?")   # no two adjacent digit runs: linear
TOP_KEY = re.compile(r"^([^\s:#'\"][^:#]*|'[^']+'|\"[^\"]+\"):(?:\s|$)")   # greedy, no backtracking across spaces
MAX_LINE = 4096   # a longer line is no catalog key
REGISTRY = "contracts/feature_map.md"
PLAN_RE = re.compile(r"docs/spec/[^/]+/test_plan\.md")
PASO = re.compile(r"^#{2,4}\s*Paso\s+(\d+)\b", re.M)
COVERAGE = re.compile(r"^#{2,4}\s*Journey coverage\b.*$", re.M | re.I)
NONE_CELL = re.compile(r"none\s*[—–-]\s*\S", re.I)
OASDIFF = "1.15.2"   # the version meta CI proves (scripts/test-contract-parity.sh)
EXCLUDE = "description,examples,title,summary,extensions"   # oasdiff 1.15: documentation and x- extensions are no parity
TAIL = 15   # lines of a failed command shown
STATUS_NUM = re.compile(r"(?:\b(?:status_code|statusCode|status|StatusCode|HttpStatusCode)\s*[=:]\s*"
                        r"|\.(?:status|sendStatus|WriteHeader|code)\(\s*"
                        r"|\b(?:HTTPException|abort|ResponseStatusException|StatusCode|Status)\(\s*(?:status_code\s*=\s*)?)([1-5]\d\d)\b")
STATUS_NAMED = re.compile(r"\b(?:HTTPStatus|HttpStatus|HttpStatusCode|StatusCode)(?:\.|::)([A-Z][A-Za-z_]*[A-Za-z])\b|\bhttp\.Status([A-Z][A-Za-z]+)\b")
STATUS_DIGITS = re.compile(r"\bstatus\.HTTP_([1-5]\d\d)_[A-Z_]+|\bStatusCodes\.Status([1-5]\d\d)[A-Za-z]*")
PHRASES = {n.replace("_", ""): s.value for n, s in http.HTTPStatus.__members__.items()}
CODE_SUFFIXES = (".py", ".ts", ".tsx", ".js", ".jsx", ".mjs", ".cjs", ".go", ".rs", ".java", ".kt", ".rb", ".php", ".cs", ".scala", ".ex", ".exs")
NOT_SOURCE = ("docs/", "config/", "contracts/", ".claude/", ".context/", "scripts/gates/", "node_modules/", "vendor/")
TEST_PATH = re.compile(r"(?:^|/)(?:tests?|__tests__|e2e|spec)/|(?:^|/)test_[^/]*$|[._-](?:test|spec)\.[^/]+$|_test\.[^/]+$|Tests?\.[^/.]+$")
LEAD_STATUS = re.compile(r"^\s*((?:[1-5]\d\d|[1-5]XX)(?:\s*[,/]\s*(?:[1-5]\d\d|[1-5]XX))*)\b")


def _norm(meaning: str) -> str:
    """Case, spacing and punctuation folded — in any script (NFKC + casefold, Unicode word characters)."""
    return re.sub(r"[\W_]+", " ", unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", meaning).casefold()).strip()


def catalog(text: str) -> tuple[set[str], list[str]]:
    """(codes, problems) of the catalog's text."""
    seen: dict[str, int] = {}
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m = TOP_KEY.match(line) if len(line) <= MAX_LINE else None
        if m:
            k = m.group(1).rstrip().strip("'\"")
            seen[k] = seen.get(k, 0) + 1
    problems = [f"`{k}` is listed {n} times — one code, one entry; give the other meaning its own code" for k, n in seen.items() if n > 1]
    data = parse_yaml(text) if text.strip() else {}
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        return set(), problems + ["the catalog is not a mapping of codes (`CODE: {meaning, status}`)"]
    if not data:
        return set(), problems + ["the catalog has no entry — write one `CODE: {meaning, status}` per meaning, or remove the file"]
    by_meaning: dict[str, str] = {}
    for code, entry in ((str(k), v) for k, v in data.items()):
        meaning = entry.get("meaning") if isinstance(entry, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(meaning, str) or not _norm(meaning):
            problems.append(f"`{code}` has no meaning — write the one meaning it names")
            continue
        n = _norm(meaning)
        if n in by_meaning:
            a, b = sorted((code, by_meaning[n]))
            problems.append(f"`{a}` and `{b}` share one meaning — keep one code and point the contracts at it")
        else:
            by_meaning[n] = code
    return {str(k) for k in data}, problems


def crud(method: str, path: str) -> bool:
    """True when `method path` is CRUD-shaped (module docstring)."""
    segs = [s for s in path.split("/") if s]
    while segs and PREFIX.fullmatch(segs[0]):
        segs.pop(0)
    if not segs:
        return False
    if segs[-1].startswith("bulk-") and len(segs) > 1 and not PARAM.fullmatch(segs[-2]):
        if method not in ("post", "patch", "delete"):
            return False
        segs = segs[:-1]
        method = "bulk"
    kinds = ["p" if PARAM.fullmatch(s) else "l" for s in segs]
    if kinds[0] != "l" or any(a == b for a, b in zip(kinds, kinds[1:])):
        return False
    if method == "bulk":
        return kinds[-1] == "l"
    return method in (("get", "put", "patch", "delete") if kinds[-1] == "p" else ("get", "post"))


def openapi(doc) -> bool:
    return isinstance(doc, dict) and any(k in doc for k in ("openapi", "swagger", "paths"))   # `paths` alone: a mistyped header is still judged


def codes_of(doc, codes: set[str] | None) -> list[str]:
    """The codes clause on one parsed contract; `codes` None = no catalog, an empty set = a red catalog (unreadable or
    empty — its own row is red: the membership is not judged twice)."""
    problems = []
    named: set[str] = set()
    done: set[int] = set()
    for ptr, node in _walk(doc, "#"):
        v = node.get("x-error-codes")
        if v is None or id(v) in done:   # one list behind many aliases is judged once
            continue
        done.add(id(v))
        if not isinstance(v, list) or not all(isinstance(c, str) and c.strip() for c in v):
            problems.append(f"{ptr}: `x-error-codes` is not a list of codes — write `x-error-codes: [CODE, …]`, each code quoted if YAML reads it as a number or a boolean")
            continue
        named |= {c.strip() for c in v}
    if named and codes is None:
        problems.append(f"names {len(named)} error code(s) but there is no catalog — create {CATALOG} with one entry per meaning")
    elif named and codes:
        problems += [f"names `{c}`, which the catalog lacks — add it to {CATALOG} with its meaning, or use the existing code for that meaning"
                     for c in sorted(named - codes)]
    return problems


REQUIRED = (   # (operation, method, where: "c" collection | "i" item | the bulk segment)
    ("create", ("post",), "c"), ("list", ("get",), "c"), ("read", ("get",), "i"), ("update", ("put", "patch"), "i"),
    ("delete", ("delete",), "i"), ("bulk-create", ("post",), "bulk-create"), ("bulk-update", ("patch",), "bulk-update"),
    ("bulk-delete", ("delete",), "bulk-delete"))


def _kinds(path: str) -> list[str] | None:
    """"l" / "p" per segment after the prefix, or None when the path does not alternate from a collection."""
    segs = [s for s in path.split("/") if s]
    while segs and PREFIX.fullmatch(segs[0]):
        segs.pop(0)
    kinds = ["p" if PARAM.fullmatch(s) else "l" for s in segs]
    if not kinds or kinds[0] != "l" or any(a == b for a, b in zip(kinds, kinds[1:])):
        return None
    return kinds


def resources(paths: dict) -> dict[str, list[str]]:
    """{collection path: [its item paths]} — the resources a contract exposes."""
    keys = {str(p).rstrip("/") or "/": p for p in paths}
    below = {k.rsplit("/", 1)[0] for k in keys}   # every path that has a path under it
    out: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
    for k, raw in keys.items():
        kinds, last = _kinds(k), k.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        if kinds is None or last.startswith("bulk-"):
            continue
        if kinds[-1] == "p":
            out.setdefault(k.rsplit("/", 1)[0], []).append(raw)
            continue
        item = paths[raw] if isinstance(paths[raw], dict) else {}
        action = len(kinds) > 1 and {m for m in OPS if m in item} <= {"post"} and k not in below
        if not action:
            out.setdefault(k, [])
    return out


def _declared(item, op: str) -> bool:
    v = item.get("x-crud-exception") if isinstance(item, dict) else None
    if isinstance(v, str):
        return bool(v.strip())
    return isinstance(v, dict) and isinstance(v.get(op), str) and bool(v[op].strip())


def crud_findings(doc) -> dict[str, str]:
    """{finding key: message} — the shape and completeness clauses on one OpenAPI document."""
    paths = doc.get("paths") or {}
    if not isinstance(paths, dict):
        return {"paths": "its `paths` is not a mapping of routes — not an OpenAPI document"}
    out: dict[str, str] = {}
    for path, item in paths.items():
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            continue
        for meth in OPS:
            op = item.get(meth)
            if not isinstance(op, dict) or crud(meth, str(path)):
                continue
            reason = op.get("x-crud-exception")
            if not isinstance(reason, str) or not reason.strip():
                out[f"{meth.upper()} {path}"] = (f"{meth.upper()} {path} is outside CRUD-First and declares no reason — add `x-crud-exception: <reason>` "
                                                 "to the operation, or reshape it as a CRUD route")
    norm = {str(p).rstrip("/") or "/": p for p in paths}
    for coll, items in resources(paths).items():
        node = lambda k: paths.get(norm.get(k)) if isinstance(paths.get(norm.get(k)), dict) else {}   # noqa: E731
        holders = [node(coll)] + [paths[i] if isinstance(paths[i], dict) else {} for i in items]
        if any("$ref" in h for h in holders):
            continue   # a referenced path item lives in another file: not judged (its operations are not here); a referenced bulk path counts as present
        for name, methods, where in REQUIRED:
            nodes = [node(coll)] if where == "c" else [paths[i] if isinstance(paths[i], dict) else {} for i in items] if where == "i" else [node(f"{coll}/{where}")]
            if any("$ref" in n or isinstance(n.get(m), dict) for n in nodes for m in methods) or any(_declared(h, name) for h in holders):
                continue
            route = f"{'|'.join(m.upper() for m in methods)} {coll}" + ("/{id}" if where == "i" else f"/{where}" if where != "c" else "")
            out[f"{coll} lacks {name}"] = (f"{coll} lacks {name} ({route}) — CRUD-First is single and batch: expose it, or declare the omission on the "
                                           f"resource: `x-crud-exception: {{{name}: <reason>}}` (one string for every omission)")
    return out


def _inside(repo: Path, p: Path) -> bool:
    try:
        return p.resolve().is_relative_to(repo.resolve())
    except (OSError, RuntimeError):
        return False


def _plans(repo: Path) -> list[str]:
    """Every docs/spec/*/test_plan.md — a file or its pin (EVOL-080) — that resolves inside the repository."""
    return [r for r in documents.glob(repo, "docs/spec/*/test_plan.md")
            if _inside(repo, repo / r if (repo / r).is_file() else repo / (r + documents.PIN))]


def _doc(repo: Path, rel: str) -> str | None:
    """The artefact's text through the one reader: the file (lenient bytes) when there is one, else its pin read live."""
    p = repo / rel
    return p.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") if p.is_file() else documents.text(repo, rel)


def _unreadable(what: str, e: BaseException) -> str:
    if isinstance(e, GateFault):
        return f"cannot be read as {what} — {str(e).replace('frontmatter is not valid YAML', 'not valid YAML')}; fix its syntax"
    return f"cannot be read as {what} — nested too deep for the reader; flatten it"


def _entries(text: str | None) -> list[str]:
    """The baseline's `undeclared` list; GateFault when the text is no baseline."""
    try:
        data = json.loads(text or "")
    except ValueError as e:
        raise GateFault(f"not valid JSON ({e})") from None
    except RecursionError:
        raise GateFault("nested too deep for the reader") from None
    v = data.get("undeclared") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(v, list) or not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in v):
        raise GateFault("it must carry `undeclared`: a list of `<contract>#<finding>` strings")
    return v


def _at_base(repo: Path, base: str, f: str) -> set[str]:
    """The CRUD finding keys the base's version of contract `f` carried (none when absent or unreadable there)."""
    text = _at(repo, base, f)
    try:
        doc = _parse(text, Path(f).suffix) if text is not None else None
    except (GateFault, RecursionError):
        return set()
    return set(crud_findings(doc)) if openapi(doc) else set()


def _baseline(repo: Path, base: str | None, found: set[str], unread: set[str]) -> tuple[set[str], dict | None]:
    """(the entries that excuse a finding, the baseline's row); `unread` = contracts that could not be read (their
    entries are neither paid nor stale — the contract's own row is red)."""
    p = repo / BASELINE
    if not p.is_file():
        return set(), None
    try:
        if not _inside(repo, p):
            raise GateFault(f"it resolves outside the repository — {BASELINE} is a file of the project, never a link out")
        entries = _entries(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace"))
    except GateFault as e:
        return set(), {"id": BASELINE, "ok": False, "problems": [f"cannot be read as the CRUD baseline — {e}"], "note": ""}
    problems = []
    try:
        if not is_tracked(repo, BASELINE):
            problems.append("the baseline is on disk but git does not track it — commit it (CI reads the commit)")
    except GateFault:
        pass   # no repository: nothing tracks anything — the direct reader
    if base is not None:
        try:
            base = _reference(repo, base)   # the merge-base: what the branch forked from
        except GateFault as e:
            problems.append(f"cannot read the base's baseline — {e}")
            base = None
    if base is not None:
        text = _at(repo, base, BASELINE)
        try:
            old = set(_entries(text)) if text is not None else set()
        except GateFault:
            old = set()
        owed: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
        for e in sorted(set(entries) - old):
            f = e.split("#", 1)[0]
            sp, _, code = e[len("status:"):].rpartition("#")   # status:<path>#<code> — the code is the last segment
            if e.startswith("status:") and "\x00" not in e and ".." not in sp.split("/"):
                prior = _at(repo, base, sp)
                if code not in {st for _, st in code_statuses(prior or "")}:
                    problems.append(f"`{e}` is new since the base — the baseline only shrinks: declare the response instead")
                continue
            if not CONTRACT_RE.fullmatch(f) or "\x00" in e or ".." in f.split("/"):
                problems.append(f"`{e}` names no contract under {TREE}/** — the baseline only shrinks: remove it")
                continue
            if f not in owed:
                owed[f] = _at_base(repo, base, f)
            if e.split("#", 1)[-1] not in owed[f]:
                problems.append(f"`{e}` is new since the base — the baseline only shrinks: declare it on the contract instead")
    problems += [f"`{e}` is no longer found — the baseline only shrinks: remove it" for e in sorted(set(entries) - found)
                 if e.split("#", 1)[0] not in unread]
    good = set(entries) & found
    return good, {"id": BASELINE, "ok": not problems, "problems": problems,
                  "note": f"{len(good)} operation(s) older than the law still owed — the list only shrinks"}


def _covers(responses: set[str], status: str) -> bool:
    return status in responses or "default" in responses or f"{status[:1]}XX" in responses


def code_statuses(text: str) -> list[tuple[int, str]]:
    """(line, status) of every status literal in one source text: a number in a status position or a named constant."""
    out = []
    for m in STATUS_NUM.finditer(text):
        out.append((text.count("\n", 0, m.start()) + 1, m.group(1)))
    for m in STATUS_DIGITS.finditer(text):
        out.append((text.count("\n", 0, m.start()) + 1, m.group(1) or m.group(2)))
    for m in STATUS_NAMED.finditer(text):
        v = PHRASES.get((m.group(1) or m.group(2)).upper().replace("_", ""))
        if v is not None:
            out.append((text.count("\n", 0, m.start()) + 1, str(v)))
    return sorted(set(out))


def _named_ops(text: str, names: list[str]) -> set[str]:
    return {n for n in names if re.search(rf"(?<![A-Za-z0-9_]){re.escape(n)}(?![A-Za-z0-9_])", text)}


def statuses(repo: Path, docs: dict) -> tuple[dict[str, str], list[str]]:
    """({`status:<path>#<code>`: finding} of the code, [TC-API row problems]) against the declared responses."""
    ops: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
    for d in docs.values():
        for n, o in operations(d).items():
            if o["named"]:
                ops.setdefault(n, set()).update(o["responses"])
    plan_probs = []
    for rel in _plans(repo):
        for head, rows in _tables(_doc(repo, rel) or ""):
            low = [h.lower() for h in head]
            if low[:1] != ["id"] or "operation" not in low or "expected status" not in low:
                continue
            io, ist = low.index("operation"), low.index("expected status")
            for r in rows:
                if not (r and _bare(r[0]).startswith("TC-API-")) or len(r) <= max(io, ist):
                    continue
                m = LEAD_STATUS.match(_bare(r[ist]))
                for op in (t for t in re.split(r"[\s,;]+", _bare(r[io])) if t in ops):
                    for st in (re.split(r"\s*[,/]\s*", m.group(1)) if m else []):
                        if not _covers(ops[op], st):
                            plan_probs.append(f"{rel} {_bare(r[0])}: expects {st} from `{op}`, which its contract does not declare — declare the response, or fix the row")
    found: dict[str, str] = {}
    if not ops:
        return found, plan_probs
    names = sorted(ops, key=len, reverse=True)
    try:
        listing = tracked_files(repo)
    except GateFault:
        listing = []
    for rel in listing:
        if not rel.endswith(CODE_SUFFIXES) or rel.startswith(NOT_SOURCE) or TEST_PATH.search(rel) or not _inside(repo, repo / rel):
            continue
        try:
            text = (repo / rel).read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")   # a non-UTF-8 byte is never a skipped file
        except OSError:
            continue
        mine = _named_ops(text, names)
        if not mine:
            continue
        allowed = set().union(*(ops[n] for n in mine))
        for line, st in code_statuses(text):
            if not _covers(allowed, st):
                found.setdefault(f"status:{rel}#{st}", f"{rel}:{line}: raises {st}, which none of {', '.join(f'`{n}`' for n in sorted(mine))} declares — declare the response in the contract, or stop raising it")
    return found, plan_probs


def check(repo: Path, base: str | None = None) -> dict:
    """`base` None skips the baseline's growth check (a direct call); the profile passes the diff base."""
    cat = repo / CATALOG
    files = sorted(p.relative_to(repo).as_posix() for p in (repo / TREE).rglob("*")
                   if p.is_file() and CONTRACT_RE.fullmatch(p.relative_to(repo).as_posix())) if (repo / TREE).is_dir() else []
    if not cat.is_file() and not files:
        return {"ok": True, "na": True, "entries": [], "undeclared": [], "reason": f"no error catalog ({CATALOG}) and no contract ({TREE}/**) — nothing to judge"}
    rows, codes = [], None
    if cat.is_file():
        if not _inside(repo, cat):
            codes, problems = set(), [f"resolves outside the repository — {CATALOG} is a file of the project, never a link out"]
        else:
            try:
                codes, problems = catalog(cat.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace"))
            except (GateFault, RecursionError) as e:
                codes, problems = set(), [_unreadable("a catalog", e)]
        rows.append({"id": CATALOG, "ok": not problems, "problems": problems, "note": f"{len(codes)} code(s), one meaning each"})
    judged: list[tuple[dict, dict[str, str]]] = []
    unread: set[str] = set()
    docs: dict[str, dict] = {}
    for f in files:
        if not _inside(repo, repo / f):
            rows.append({"id": f, "ok": False, "problems": ["resolves outside the repository — a contract is a file of the project, never a link out"], "note": ""})
            continue
        try:
            doc = _load(repo / f)
            problems = codes_of(doc, codes) if isinstance(doc, dict) else []
            found = {f"{f}#{k}": m for k, m in crud_findings(doc).items()} if openapi(doc) else {}
        except (GateFault, RecursionError) as e:
            doc, problems, found = None, [_unreadable("a contract", e)], {}
            unread.add(f)
        row = {"id": f, "problems": problems, "note": "every code in the catalog; " + (
            "CRUD-First single and batch, kept or declared" if openapi(doc) else "CRUD not judged — not an OpenAPI document")}
        rows.append(row)
        judged.append((row, found))
        if openapi(doc):
            docs[f] = doc
    found = {k for _, fd in judged for k in fd}
    st_found, st_plan = statuses(repo, docs) if docs else ({}, [])
    found |= set(st_found)
    excused, brow = _baseline(repo, base, found, unread)
    for row, fd in judged:
        row["problems"] += [m for k, m in fd.items() if k not in excused]
        owed = len([k for k in fd if k in excused])
        if owed:
            row["note"] += f"; {owed} older than the law, in the baseline"
        row["ok"] = not row["problems"]
    if docs:
        owed = [k for k in st_found if k in excused]
        rows.append({"id": "statuses", "ok": False, "problems": st_plan + [m for k, m in sorted(st_found.items()) if k not in excused],
                     "note": "every expected and raised status is a declared response" + (f"; {len(owed)} older than the law, in the baseline" if owed else "")})
        rows[-1]["ok"] = not rows[-1]["problems"]
    if brow:
        rows.append(brow)
    reg = registry(repo, dict(docs))
    rows += ([reg] if reg else []) + _plan_rows(repo, base, docs)
    red = [r for r in rows if not r["ok"]]
    return {"ok": not red, "entries": rows, "undeclared": sorted(found),
            "reason": f"{len(red)} of {len(rows)} file(s) red" if red else f"{len(rows)} file(s) green — one code per meaning, CRUD-First single and batch"}


# ─── parity (EVOL-070) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def _cells(line: str) -> list[str]:
    return [c.strip() for c in line.strip().strip("|").split("|")]


def _tables(text: str):
    """(header cells, [row cells]) of every markdown table outside code fences."""
    head, rows, fence = None, [], False
    for line in text.splitlines() + [""]:
        if line.lstrip().startswith(("```", "~~~")):
            fence = not fence
        is_row = not fence and line.lstrip().startswith("|")
        if is_row and head is None:
            head = _cells(line)
        elif is_row and not set(line.replace("|", "").strip()) <= set(":- "):
            rows.append(_cells(line))
        elif not is_row and head is not None:
            yield head, rows
            head, rows = None, []


def _bare(cell: str) -> str:
    return cell.replace("`", "").strip()


def _local(doc, node):
    """A `{"$ref": "#/…"}` node resolved inside its document (one hop per level, bounded); anything else as it is."""
    for _ in range(8):
        ref = node.get("$ref") if isinstance(node, dict) else None
        if not (isinstance(ref, str) and ref.startswith("#/")):
            return node
        node = doc
        for part in ref[2:].split("/"):
            node = node.get(part.replace("~1", "/").replace("~0", "~")) if isinstance(node, dict) else None
    return node


def operations(doc, dupes: list | None = None) -> dict[str, dict]:
    """operationId (or `METHOD path` when it has none) → {key, named, responses, codes (None = lists none)}; a local
    `$ref` response is read where it points. A second operation under one operationId is appended to `dupes`."""
    out: dict[str, dict] = {}
    paths = doc.get("paths") if isinstance(doc, dict) else None
    for path, item in (paths.items() if isinstance(paths, dict) else []):
        for m in OPS:
            op = item.get(m) if isinstance(item, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(op, dict):
                continue
            oid = op.get("operationId")
            named = isinstance(oid, str) and bool(oid.strip())
            resp = op.get("responses")
            resp = resp if isinstance(resp, dict) else {}
            listed = [v for r in resp.values() for _, n in _walk(_local(doc, r)) for v in [n.get("x-error-codes")] if isinstance(v, list)]
            name = oid.strip() if named else f"{m.upper()} {path}"
            if name in out and dupes is not None:
                dupes.append(name)
            out[name] = {"key": f"{m.upper()} {path}", "named": named, "responses": {str(k) for k in resp},
                         "codes": {c.strip() for v in listed for c in v if isinstance(c, str)} if listed else None}
    return out


def registry(repo: Path, docs: dict) -> dict | None:
    """The registry clause: every ACTIVE row of contracts/feature_map.md states its contract's info.version."""
    p = repo / REGISTRY
    if not p.is_file():
        return None
    if not _inside(repo, p):
        return {"id": REGISTRY, "ok": False, "problems": ["resolves outside the repository — the registry is a file of the project"], "note": ""}
    problems, n = [], 0
    for head, rows in _tables(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")):
        low = [h.lower() for h in head]
        if "contract path" not in low:
            continue
        if "version" not in low:
            problems.append("its table has no `Version` column — add it: each row states its contract's `info.version` (SETUP --upgrade fills it)")
            continue
        ip, iv, ist = low.index("contract path"), low.index("version"), low.index("status") if "status" in low else None
        for r in rows:
            cell = _bare(r[ip]) if len(r) > ip else ""
            if not cell or (ist is not None and len(r) > ist and _bare(r[ist]).upper() not in ("ACTIVE", "")):
                continue
            f = cell.split()[0]
            f = f if f.startswith("contracts/") else f"contracts/{f}"
            if not CONTRACT_RE.fullmatch(f):   # GraphQL, proto, AsyncAPI: no info.version this reader reads — the cell states —
                if not (repo / f).is_file() or not _inside(repo, repo / f):
                    problems.append(f"a row names `{f}`, which is no file of the project — fix the path or mark the row SUPERSEDED")
                continue
            if f not in docs:
                full = repo / f
                if not full.is_file() or not _inside(repo, full):
                    problems.append(f"a row names `{f}`, which is no file of the project — fix the path or mark the row SUPERSEDED")
                    continue
                try:
                    docs[f] = _load(full)
                except (GateFault, RecursionError) as e:
                    problems.append(f"a row names `{f}`, which {_unreadable('a contract', e)}")
                    continue
            info = docs[f].get("info") if isinstance(docs[f], dict) else None
            want = info.get("version") if isinstance(info, dict) else None
            want = None if want is None else (str(want) if isinstance(want, str) else None)
            if want is None and isinstance(info, dict) and info.get("version") is not None:
                problems.append(f"`{f}`: info.version is not a string — quote it (`version: \"1.10\"`), YAML reads 1.10 as 1.1")
                continue
            if want is None:
                continue   # a contract without info.version (GraphQL, proto): no version to state
            n += 1
            got = _bare(r[iv]) if len(r) > iv else ""
            got = got[1:] if got[:1] in ("v", "V") else got
            if got != str(want).strip():
                problems.append(f"`{f}` is at {want} but its row states {got or 'no version'} — write the contract's info.version in the row")
    return {"id": REGISTRY, "ok": not problems, "problems": problems, "note": f"{n} row(s), each at its contract's info.version"}


def _base_ops(repo: Path, ref: str) -> set[str]:
    names: set[str] = set()
    for f in tree_entries(repo, ref):
        if CONTRACT_RE.fullmatch(f):
            text = _at(repo, ref, f)
            try:
                doc = _parse(text, Path(f).suffix) if text is not None else None
            except (GateFault, RecursionError):
                continue   # unreadable at the base: its operations count as new — the safe side
            names |= set(operations(doc)) if openapi(doc) else set()
    return names


def _plan_ops(repo: Path) -> set[str]:
    """Every operation a TC-API row names, in any docs/spec/*/test_plan.md (the `Operation` cell of an ID table)."""
    out: set[str] = set()
    for rel in _plans(repo):
        for head, rows in _tables(_doc(repo, rel) or ""):
            low = [h.lower() for h in head]
            if low[:1] == ["id"] and "operation" in low:
                i = low.index("operation")
                out |= {t for r in rows if len(r) > i and _bare(r[0]).startswith("TC-API-") for t in re.split(r"[\s,;]+", _bare(r[i])) if t}
    return out


def _changed(repo: Path, ref: str) -> set[str]:
    """Paths changed since `ref`: committed, staged, unstaged and untracked (the static round runs before `git add`)."""
    return {p for p in (_git(repo, "diff", "--name-only", "--no-renames", ref).splitlines()
                        + _git(repo, "ls-files", "--others", "--exclude-standard").splitlines()) if p}


def coverage(text: str, journey: str, names: set[str]) -> list[str]:
    """The journey clause on one test plan: every Paso of its journey covered, each cell an operation or a reason."""
    pasos = sorted({str(int(n)) for n in PASO.findall(journey)}, key=int)
    if not pasos:
        return []
    m = COVERAGE.search(text)
    if not m:
        return [f"its journey has {len(pasos)} step(s) and the plan has no `### Journey coverage` — add `| Paso | Operation |`, one row per step"]
    section = text[m.end():]
    nxt = re.search(r"^#{1,4}\s", section, re.M)
    rows = next(_tables(section[:nxt.start()] if nxt else section), (None, []))[1]
    problems, seen = [], set()
    for r in rows:
        num = re.search(r"\d+", r[0]) if r else None
        if not num:
            continue
        seen.add(str(int(num.group())))
        cell = _bare(r[1]) if len(r) > 1 else ""
        if NONE_CELL.match(cell):
            continue
        bad = [t for t in re.split(r"[\s,;]+", cell) if t and t not in names]
        if not cell or bad:
            problems.append(f"Paso {int(num.group())}: `{cell or '(empty)'}` is no operation of the contracts — name an operationId, or write `none — <reason>`")
    problems += [f"Paso {n} has no coverage row — name the operation that serves it, or `none — <reason>`" for n in pasos if n not in seen]
    return problems


def _plan_rows(repo: Path, base: str | None, docs: dict) -> list[dict]:
    """The change-scoped clauses: one contract test per new operation, the journey coverage of a changed plan."""
    if base is None:
        return []
    try:
        ref = _reference(repo, base)
        names = {n for d in docs.values() for n in operations(d)}
        new = names - _base_ops(repo, ref)
        changed = documents.artefacts(sorted(_changed(repo, ref)))   # a changed pin is a changed plan (EVOL-080)
    except GateFault as e:
        return [{"id": "contract tests", "ok": False, "problems": [f"cannot read the base — {e}"], "note": ""}]
    planned, rows = _plan_ops(repo), []
    named = {n for d in docs.values() for n, o in operations(d).items() if o["named"]}
    unnamed = sorted(n for n in new if n not in named)
    missing = sorted(n for n in new if n in named and n not in planned)
    problems = [f"`{n}` is new and has no operationId — name it: the contract test and its record speak by operationId" for n in unnamed]
    problems += [f"`{n}` is new and no TC-API row names it — add the row (its `Operation` cell `{n}`) to the feature's test_plan.md: "
                 "one red contract test per operation before the build (CONTRACT-FREEZE)" for n in missing]
    rows.append({"id": "contract tests", "ok": not problems, "problems": problems,
                 "note": f"{len(new)} new operation(s), each named by a TC-API row"})
    for f in sorted(p for p in changed if PLAN_RE.fullmatch(p)):
        j = f.replace("test_plan.md", "user_journey.md")
        if not all(documents.exists(repo, r) and _inside(repo, repo / r if (repo / r).is_file() else repo / (r + documents.PIN)) for r in (f, j)):
            continue
        problems = coverage(_doc(repo, f), _doc(repo, j), names)
        rows.append({"id": f, "ok": not problems, "problems": problems, "note": "every journey step covered by an operation or a reason"})
    return rows


def _timeout(repo: Path) -> int:
    t = key(repo, "contracts.timeout_s", default=1800)
    if type(t) is not int or t <= 0:
        raise GateFault(f"config/quality.json → contracts.timeout_s is {t!r} — a positive number of seconds")
    return t


def _run(repo: Path, cmd: str, env: dict | None = None) -> tuple[int, str]:
    """A command the project declared (config/quality.json), in its own session so a timeout stops its whole tree."""
    import os
    import signal
    limit = _timeout(repo)
    p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, shell=True, cwd=repo, env={**os.environ, **(env or {})}, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,  # nosemgrep: python-shell-non-literal — the project's declared contract-test / emit command (config), paths quoted
                         stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True, errors="replace", start_new_session=True)
    try:
        out, _ = p.communicate(timeout=limit)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        try:
            os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            pass
        try:
            p.communicate(timeout=10)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:   # a descendant left the session holding the pipe: stop reading, report
            pass
        return 124, f"timed out after {limit} s (contracts.timeout_s)"
    return p.returncode, "\n".join(out.strip().splitlines()[-TAIL:])


def _fresh(state: Path, name: str) -> Path:
    """An empty `state/name`, never through a link: a link on the way, a file in the way or a failed clean is a fault."""
    for d in (state, state / name):
        if d.is_symlink():
            raise GateFault(f"{d} is a link — the parity state is a plain folder; remove the link and run again")
    d = state / name
    try:
        if d.exists() and not d.is_dir():
            d.unlink()
        shutil.rmtree(d) if d.exists() else None
        d.mkdir(parents=True)
    except OSError as e:
        raise GateFault(f"cannot prepare {d} — {e.strerror or e}") from e
    return d


def _test_files(repo: Path, root: str) -> list[str]:
    base = repo / root
    return sorted(p.relative_to(repo).as_posix() for p in base.rglob("*") if p.is_file() and not p.is_symlink() and _inside(repo, p))


def _observed(repo: Path, obs: Path, ops: dict, codes: set[str] | None) -> list[str]:
    raw = key(repo, "contracts.tests_root", default="tests/api")
    root = raw.strip() if isinstance(raw, str) else ""
    if not root or Path(root).is_absolute() or ".." in Path(root).parts:
        return [f"`contracts.tests_root` is {raw!r} — a folder of the project, relative to its root"]
    root = root.strip("/")
    if not (repo / root).is_dir() or not _inside(repo, repo / root):
        return [f"no contract tests under `{root}` (`contracts.tests_root`) — the TC-API tests live there, each recording its answers"]
    runs = _scoped(repo, _test_files(repo, root))["runs"]
    if not runs:
        return [f"no file under `{root}` is a test a `verification.gates` row with `scoped` runs (its red_reads, else traceability.test_roots)"]
    for r in runs:
        rc, out = _run(repo, r["command"], {"CONTRACT_OBSERVED": str(obs)})
        if rc != 0:
            return [f"the contract tests failed (`{r['gate']}`, exit {rc}) — fix them first:\n{out}"]
    lines = [(f.name, ln) for f in sorted(obs.glob("*.jsonl")) if f.is_file() and not f.is_symlink()
             for ln in f.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    if not lines:
        return ["the contract tests recorded nothing in CONTRACT_OBSERVED — each response appends one line (develop/api_test_template.md § Recording the answers)"]
    problems, seen = [], set()
    for name, ln in lines:
        try:
            o = json.loads(ln)
        except (ValueError, RecursionError):
            o = None
        if not (isinstance(o, dict) and isinstance(o.get("operation"), str) and type(o.get("status")) is int
                and (o.get("code") is None or isinstance(o.get("code"), str))):
            problems.append(f"{name}: `{ln[:120]}` is no record — write {{\"operation\": \"<operationId>\", \"status\": <int>, \"code\": \"<CODE>\"|null}}")
            continue
        op, status, code = o["operation"], str(o["status"]), o.get("code")
        if op not in ops or not ops[op]["named"]:
            problems.append(f"`{op}` answered and no contract declares it — name the operationId the contract gives")
            continue
        seen.add(op)
        declared = ops[op]["responses"]
        if status not in declared and "default" not in declared and f"{status[:1]}XX" not in declared:
            problems.append(f"`{op}` answered {status} and its contract does not declare it — declare the response, or stop raising it")
        if code and (codes is None or code not in codes):
            problems.append(f"`{op}` answered code `{code}`, which the catalog lacks — add it to {CATALOG}, one meaning each")
        elif code and ops[op]["codes"] is not None and code not in ops[op]["codes"]:
            problems.append(f"`{op}` answered code `{code}` outside its `x-error-codes` — list it on the operation")
    problems += [f"`{n}` was never answered by a contract test — one contract test per operation" for n in sorted(set(ops) - seen) if ops[n]["named"]]
    problems += [f"`{n}` has no operationId — name it: a contract test records by operationId" for n in sorted(ops) if not ops[n]["named"]]
    return problems


def _comparable(doc: dict, openapi_line) -> dict:
    """What parity compares: no servers, no tags, the authored `openapi` line — an emitter's deployment and grouping
    choices are no contract."""
    d = copy.deepcopy(doc)
    d.pop("servers", None)
    d.pop("tags", None)
    d["openapi"] = openapi_line
    for item in (d.get("paths") or {}).values() if isinstance(d.get("paths"), dict) else []:
        for m in OPS + ("head", "options", "trace"):
            if isinstance(item, dict) and isinstance(item.get(m), dict):
                item[m].pop("tags", None)
                item[m].pop("servers", None)
        if isinstance(item, dict):
            item.pop("servers", None)
    return d


def _emit_ready(repo: Path) -> tuple[str | None, str | None, list[str]]:
    emit = key(repo, "contracts.emit")
    if not isinstance(emit, str) or "{out}" not in emit:
        return None, None, ["`contracts.emit` is not declared — write the command that emits the code's OpenAPI under `{out}` (rules/contract-first-policy.md "
                            "§ Contract parity names your framework's emitter); a framework with none carries a dated skip of `contract-parity`"]
    tool = shutil.which("oasdiff")
    if tool is None:
        return None, None, [f"oasdiff is not installed — install oasdiff {OASDIFF} (rules/contract-first-policy.md § Contract parity): the parity is never green unproven"]
    return emit, tool, []


def _emitted(repo: Path, out: Path, cmp: Path, docs: dict, emit: str, tool: str) -> list[str]:
    rc, msg = _run(repo, emit.replace("{out}", shlex.quote(str(out))))
    if rc != 0:
        return [f"`contracts.emit` failed (exit {rc}):\n{msg}"]
    twins: dict[str, list[Path]] = {}
    for p in out.rglob("*"):
        if p.is_file() and not p.is_symlink() and p.suffix in (".json", ".yaml", ".yml"):
            twins.setdefault(p.relative_to(out).with_suffix("").as_posix(), []).append(p)
    problems, want = [], set()
    for f in sorted(docs):
        stem = Path(f).relative_to(TREE).with_suffix("").as_posix()
        want.add(stem)
        if stem not in twins:
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: the code emits no `{stem}` — the contract declares what the code does not expose")
            continue
        if len(twins[stem]) > 1:
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: the code emits {len(twins[stem])} documents for `{stem}` — one twin per contract")
            continue
        try:
            emitted = _load(twins[stem][0])
        except (GateFault, RecursionError) as e:
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: the emitted twin {_unreadable('an OpenAPI document', e)}")
            continue
        if not isinstance(emitted, dict):
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: the emitted twin is no OpenAPI document")
            continue
        a, b = cmp / f"{len(want)}-authored.json", cmp / f"{len(want)}-emitted.json"
        try:   # a YAML date or time is compared as its text; a document that refers to itself is no contract
            a.write_text(json.dumps(_comparable(docs[f], docs[f].get("openapi")), default=str), encoding="utf-8")
            b.write_text(json.dumps(_comparable(emitted, docs[f].get("openapi")), default=str), encoding="utf-8")
        except (TypeError, ValueError, RecursionError) as e:
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: cannot be compared ({_clean(str(e))[:120]}) — a contract is a tree, with no anchor that refers to itself")
            continue
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([tool, "diff", str(a), str(b), "--fail-on-diff", "--allow-external-refs=false",
                                "--exclude-elements", EXCLUDE, "--format", "text"], capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace",
                               timeout=_timeout(repo))
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: oasdiff could not run — {e}")
            continue
        if r.returncode == 1:
            problems.append(f"`{f}` differs from what the code emits — align the code or the contract:\n" + "\n".join(r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[:40]))
        elif r.returncode != 0:
            problems.append(f"`{f}`: oasdiff could not compare (exit {r.returncode}) — {(r.stderr.strip().splitlines() or ['no message'])[-1]}")
    problems += [f"the code emits `{s}` and no contract declares it — write contracts/openapi/{s}.yaml or stop exposing it" for s in sorted(set(twins) - want)]
    return problems


def parity(repo: Path) -> dict:
    """The loop member `contract-parity`: what the code answers and emits against what the contracts declare."""
    docs: dict[str, dict] = {}
    rows = []
    files = sorted(p.relative_to(repo).as_posix() for p in (repo / TREE).rglob("*")
                   if p.is_file() and CONTRACT_RE.fullmatch(p.relative_to(repo).as_posix())) if (repo / TREE).is_dir() else []
    for f in files:
        if not _inside(repo, repo / f):
            rows.append({"id": f, "ok": False, "problems": ["resolves outside the repository — a contract is a file of the project"], "note": ""})
            continue
        try:
            doc = _load(repo / f)
        except (GateFault, RecursionError) as e:
            rows.append({"id": f, "ok": False, "problems": [_unreadable("a contract", e)], "note": ""})
            continue
        if openapi(doc) and isinstance(doc.get("paths"), dict):
            docs[f] = doc
    if not docs and not rows:
        return {"ok": True, "na": True, "entries": [], "reason": f"no OpenAPI contract under {TREE}/** — nothing to compare"}
    ops: dict[str, dict] = {}
    dupes: list[str] = []
    for f, d in docs.items():
        mine: list[str] = []
        for n, o in operations(d, mine).items():
            if n in ops:   # the same operationId in two contracts (v1 and v2): one record serves both, each declaring it
                ops[n]["responses"] |= o["responses"]
                ops[n]["codes"] = None if ops[n]["codes"] is None or o["codes"] is None else ops[n]["codes"] | o["codes"]
            else:
                ops[n] = {**o, "responses": set(o["responses"])}
        dupes += [f"`{n}` names two operations of {f} — an operationId is unique in its document (OpenAPI)" for n in sorted(set(mine))]
    if dupes:
        rows.append({"id": "operationIds", "ok": False, "problems": dupes, "note": ""})
    cat = repo / CATALOG
    codes = None
    if cat.is_file() and _inside(repo, cat):
        try:
            codes = catalog(cat.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace"))[0]
        except (GateFault, RecursionError):
            codes = set()
    emit, tool, p = _emit_ready(repo)
    if p:
        rows.append({"id": "emitted", "ok": False, "problems": p, "note": ""})
    state = _state_dir(repo, vcfg(repo)["dir"]) / "contract-parity"
    if state.is_symlink():
        raise GateFault(f"{state} is a link — the parity state is a plain folder; remove the link and run again")
    try:
        state.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    except OSError as e:
        raise GateFault(f"{state} cannot be the parity state folder ({e.strerror or e}) — remove what is in the way and run again") from e
    p = _observed(repo, _fresh(state, "observed"), ops, codes)
    rows.append({"id": "observed", "ok": not p, "problems": p, "note": f"{len(ops)} operation(s) answered, every status and code declared"})
    if emit:
        p = _emitted(repo, _fresh(state, "emitted"), _fresh(state, "compared"), docs, emit, tool)
        rows.append({"id": "emitted", "ok": not p, "problems": p, "note": f"{len(docs)} contract(s) equal to what the code emits"})
    red = [r for r in rows if not r["ok"]]
    return {"ok": not red, "entries": rows,
            "reason": f"{len(red)} of {len(rows)} check(s) red" if red else "the code answers and emits what the contracts declare"}


def render(res: dict) -> str:
    if not res.get("entries"):
        return _clean(f"contracts: {'n/a' if res['ok'] else 'RED'} — {res['reason']}")
    lines = [f"contracts: {'ok' if res['ok'] else 'RED'} — {res['reason']}"]
    for r in res["entries"]:
        lines += [f"  ✓ {r['id']}: {r['note']}"] if r["ok"] else [f"  ✗ {r['id']}: {p}" for p in r["problems"]]
    return "\n".join(_clean(part) for ln in lines for part in ln.split("\n"))
